  "source_contract": [
    "Current pinned IVec2 input constructors install no special validator or unit control. NodeValue defaults to constant unit mode 0.",
    "IVec2 valueProcess rounds the first two components after optional units, including getValue(time,false).",
    "Depth-two rows use array_verify_new(row,2); scalar rows become zeros, short rows extend and long rows truncate. Deeper inputs are not converted by the source getter.",
    "Source stores unit mode in the top-level input record. Native import admits absent/unit=0 and retains unsupported or malformed modes as opaque source nodes."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Round supported numeric IVec2 scalar and coordinate array carriers with source half-even rounding after PCX, preserving raw authored storage.",
    "Handle native flat pairs, packed vector rows, legacy nested rows and bounded PCX Items carriers.",
    "Refuse deeper rows before truncation, including discarded tails; preserve original input views and payloads on refusal.",
    "Validate PXC constant-unit mapping and source retention for nonconstant or malformed unit records."
  ],
